      "title": "Qt: Don't allow tap dialogs to apply with no capture file",
      "message": "Qt: Don't allow tap dialogs to apply with no capture file\n\ntap dialogs disable the edit and apply button after the\ncapture file is closed. Also check if the capture file is\nvalid (\"open, readable, and tappable\") and disable the buttons\nin that case as well. We don't get the closed signal if the\ndialog is initially opened with no capture file. Perform the\ncheck upon dialog creation.\n\nThis prevents some heap-use-after-free and garbage entries in\nthe tap (e.g., SRT) tables if the Apply button is pushed when\nthe dialog was opened with no capture file opened.\n\nWe could (should?) disable the various tap dialog menu items\nelsewhere too (WiresharkMainWindow::setMenusForCaptureFile ?)\nwhen no capture file is open.\n",
